findings.body:
`TabDisplayView.scrollToTab` still builds `IndexPath(row: scrollState.toIndex, section: 1)`. The PR removed the inactive-tabs section, so the tabs section is now index 0 (see `updateSnapshot` appending only `.tabs`). The `isValid(indexPath:)` guard on line 176 returns early for section 1, so scroll-to-selected-tab and scroll-to-tab silently stop working with no crash or log. The XCUI test identifiers were updated from `_1_1` to `_0_1`, which confirms the section index moved to 0, but this code path was missed.

::diff{file="firefox-ios/Client/Frontend/Browser/Tabs/Views/TabDisplayView.swift" lines="171-180"}

::callout{type="warning"}
Because the guard silently drops the scroll, this is easy to miss in manual testing when the selected tab is already visible. It only shows up when the selected tab is off-screen.

::

When no tab is selected, `createTabScrollBehavior` used to scroll to the last tab with `tabs.count - 1`. This PR changes it to `state.tabs.count`, which is one past the last valid index. The downstream `isValid(indexPath:)` guard drops the scroll, so the tab tray no longer lands on the most recent tab when switching panels. The unit test `testCreateTabScrollBehavior_forScrollToSelectedTab_noSelectedTab_returnsLastTab_ifTabsNotEmpty` still asserts `tabCount - 1` (TabsPanelStateTests.swift:152), so this test will fail. The change looks like an accidental edit of the tests' expected value during the refactor, or an unintended change to the reducer.

::diff{file="firefox-ios/Client/Frontend/Browser/Tabs/State/TabsPanelState.swift" lines="136-144"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The test file in the diff keeps `XCTAssertEqual(scrollState?.toIndex, tabCount - 1, ...)`, so the test and the code now disagree. Either the test or the code is wrong, and the test expectation (last tab) is the intended behavior per the comment above.

::

The diff deletes the three-line MPL license header at the top of `TabPanelAction.swift`. This is a live file (it still defines `TabPanelViewAction`, `TabPanelViewActionType` and `TabPanelMiddlewareAction`), so this is not a deletion of the whole file. Other files in the same directory keep the header, and the repo's lint/licence checks expect it. The change looks like it was made by accident, probably from a copy/paste during the action cleanup.

::diff{file="firefox-ios/Client/Frontend/Browser/Tabs/Action/TabPanelAction.swift" lines="1-3"}

::callout{type="info"}
The removal is unrelated to inactive tabs and should not be bundled into a feature-removal PR.

::

The PR's goal is to remove the inactive tabs feature, but the four strings in the `InactiveTabs` block were relocated into a new `struct v147` rather than deleted. Nothing in the codebase references `v147` or the `TabsTrayInactiveTabsSectionClosedAccessibilityTitle` / `CloseAllInactiveTabsButton` / `CloseInactiveTabSwipeActionTitle` members after this PR, so they are dead code. `TabsTrayInactiveTabsSectionTitle` (Strings.swift:7879) is also left unused. The `v147` name also does not follow the repo's convention, where version suffixes live on the localization keys, not on Swift type names. Keeping these strings also means the localization pipeline keeps shipping translations for removed UI.

::diff{file="firefox-ios/Shared/Strings.swift" lines="8461-8484"}

::callout{type="info"}
If the team wants to keep these keys around for a localization-freeze reason, that should be a conscious decision and noted in the PR description.

::
